  "notes": "Transcribed 2026-09-30 from the official Ramapo College of New Jersey 'Computer Science - Recommended Graduation Plan (Fall 2025)' page (ramapo.edu/recommended-graduation-plan-2025/tas/computer-science/), stated applicable to students admitted to the major during the 2025-2026 academic year. True degree is the BS in Computer Science (Ramapo awards the BS; the 4+1 variants state 'GPA Required for BS in Computer Science: 2.0'). Course titles/credits taken from the plan page and its official catalog.ramapo.edu course links; transcription method: manual transcription of each printed semester row. Sequence printed totals are 16 credits x 8 terms = 128, which matches the catalog degree minimum of 128 credits - no discrepancy. 0-credit PATH career-pathway modules (TS1/TS2/TS3) are degree requirements and are marked required_zero. Choice slots: MATH 237 vs MATH 205 (WI) option; CMPS Elective x6; MATH Elective x2; General Education Requirement x7 (any Gen Ed in any order except INTD 101/CRWT/MATH first; must include Social Science Inquiry (+W), Scientific Reasoning, Historical Perspectives (+W), Studies in the Arts & Humanities (+W), Global Awareness (+W), two Distribution categories, one outside TAS); Free Elective x3 (minor/certificate/second major). WI = Writing Intensive (3 required in the major): CMPS 311, CMPS 450, and MATH 205 (if chosen). CRWT 101->102 and MATH 021/022->024->110-121 placement is determined by placement testing; sequence assumes placement into MATH 110 and CRWT 102. No standalone plain-CS Fall 2026 (2026-2027) sequence was published at collection time - only 4+1 variants - so the 2025-2026 plan is the most current official term-by-term source.",
